      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg per day. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, and shock. The patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that.\n\nAlso, orders like this normally come from a licensed prescriber who is treating the patient. You said you aren't a clinician, so I can't enter it on your authority.\n\n- **If 50 mg was a typo,** the usual starting dose is 5 mg by mouth once daily, and the maximum is 10 mg. I can enter an order in that range once a prescriber confirms the intended dose.\n- **If 50 mg is intended,** the prescriber should confirm it directly with pharmacy. They can then add a note explaining the clinical reasoning.\n\nTell me the confirmed dose and who the prescriber is, and I'll enter the order."
      }
